; THE KEY SCHEDULE AND THE TABLE SWAP  which is everything an inverse cipher
; has to do ONCE  however many blocks it goes on to decrypt;
;
; It runs the schedule FORWARD against the forward S box  keeping the ten
; temps the regression will need; then it clears that table and writes the
; INVERSE one into the same cells; It leaves the pointer at the block's own
; zero  the inverse table resident  the last round key in the regression
; window and the ten temps standing;
;
; THIS IS WHY CBC DECRYPTION TOOK A RESTRUCTURING AND THE OTHER MODES DID NOT;
; the forward cipher splits into a table that is laid once and rounds that run
; many times  because its table SURVIVES a block; this one's does not  it is
; swapped halfway through  so there is no prefix of the single file that a
; caller could run once; Splitting it here is what makes the swap a once per
; message cost instead of a once per block one; At about sixty six thousand
; instructions to clear the forward table and seventeen more to write the
; inverse  that is the difference between a mode that is usable and one that
; is not;
;
; THE SPLIT FALLS WHERE IT DOES SO THE INSTRUCTION STREAM DOES NOT MOVE; the
; inverse table's walk home ends at nought and the per block work opens at
; nought  so the two concatenated are byte for byte the file they came from
; and aes/decrypt128 regenerates identical; That is the same test the forward
; split passed and the same reason the seam is where it is;
;
; WHAT A SECOND BLOCK MUST PUT BACK; the rounds next door REGRESS the window
; and SPEND the ten temps  so a caller decrypting more than one block has to
; keep a copy of both and restore them before each; That is fifty six bytes
; against a hundred and fourteen million instructions  and the rounds' own
; entry contracts police everything else;
;
; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE and the include's offset resolves them;
;
; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero)
;   @0x057:0x07e  the temp run{40}  ten four byte schedule temps  WANTED AGAIN
;   @0x0a0:0x0af  window{16}  the last round key  WANTED AGAIN
;   @0x0b0:0x0bf  window{16}  phase one's own  spent  and cleared next door
;   @0x0f3:0x3f5  group 0 and the table  forward  then INVERSE

; ==== phase one : the key schedule  with the FORWARD table ====
; the first four words ARE the key and they stay in the window; the earlier
; cut also copied them into a 176 byte schedule  which is gone

; ==== the forward S box is written into the tape ====
  R246
; ASSERT ptr=+246
%%block/sbox256%%
; ASSERT ptr=+1011
  L1011
; ASSERT ptr=+0
; the round constant starts at one
  R237+L237

; ten groups of four words
  ++++++++++
  [-

